  "orig_coordinate_geometry_straight_lines": {
    "starters": [
      {
        "id": "line-intersection-and-area",
        "title": "Find a line, its intersection and its intercept area",
        "marks": 7,
        "question": "<p>The line \\(l\\) passes through \\(A(-2,5)\\) and \\(B(4,2)\\).</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find an equation of \\(l\\). <strong>[3]</strong></li><li>Find the intersection of \\(l\\) with \\(y=x+1\\). <strong>[2]</strong></li><li>Find the area of the triangle bounded by \\(l\\) and the axes. <strong>[2]</strong></li></ol>",
        "solution": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>The gradient is \\((2-5)/(4-(-2))=-\\tfrac12\\). Using \\(A\\) gives \\(y-5=-\\tfrac12(x+2)\\), so \\(l\\) is \\(y=4-\\tfrac12x\\). <strong>[3]</strong></li><li>From \\(4-\\tfrac12x=x+1\\), find \\(x=2\\) and \\(y=3\\). The intersection is \\((2,3)\\). <strong>[2]</strong></li><li>The intercepts are \\((8,0)\\) and \\((0,4)\\). The area is \\(\\tfrac12(8)(4)=16\\) square units. <strong>[2]</strong></li></ol>"
      },
      {
        "id": "distance-to-a-line",
        "title": "Meet a perpendicular and find the exact distance",
        "marks": 7,
        "question": "<p>The line \\(l\\) has equation \\(x+2y=8\\). A line \\(m\\) goes through \\(P(3,-2)\\) perpendicular to \\(l\\).</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find an equation of \\(m\\). <strong>[2]</strong></li><li>Find the intersection \\(H\\) of \\(l\\) and \\(m\\). <strong>[3]</strong></li><li>Find the exact length \\(PH\\). <strong>[2]</strong></li></ol>",
        "solution": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>The gradient of \\(l\\) is \\(-\\tfrac12\\). The perpendicular through \\(P\\) is \\(y+2=2(x-3)\\), or \\(y=2x-8\\). <strong>[2]</strong></li><li>Substitute into \\(x+2y=8\\) to get \\(5x=24\\). The point is \\(H=(\\tfrac{24}5,\\tfrac85)\\). <strong>[3]</strong></li><li>The coordinate changes are \\(\\tfrac95\\) and \\(\\tfrac{18}5\\). Hence \\(PH=9\\sqrt5/5\\). <strong>[2]</strong></li></ol>"
      }
    ],
